  "content": [
    {
      "id": "introduction",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A simple but <b>powerful technique for problems</b> that ask you about a subarray of fixed length like \"find the maximum sum of any 3 consecutive elements.",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1-the-problem-first",
      "title": "1. The Problem First",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Suppose you have this array and you need to find the&nbsp;<strong>maximum sum of any 3 consecutive elements</strong>:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250876377-161373998.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250876377-161373998.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250876377-161373998.png",
          "alt": "Array for finding max sum of 3 consecutive elements"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A beginner might check every possible group of 3 elements and calculate the sum each time. This works, but it is inefficient.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "1. Brute Force Approach",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For every starting index, calculate the sum of the next 3 elements from scratch. This causes many repeated additions.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Time Complexity:</strong>&nbsp;O(n × k)",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "2. Sliding Window Approach",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "First calculate the sum of the initial window of 3 elements. Then move the window forward by subtracting the element that leaves the window and adding the new element that enters it.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Time Complexity:</strong>&nbsp;O(n)",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-the-core-idea",
      "title": "2. The Core Idea",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Think of a physical window frame sliding along the array. The window always shows exactly&nbsp;<strong>k</strong>&nbsp;elements. As it moves one step right:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "One element&nbsp;<strong>leaves</strong>&nbsp;from the left",
            "One element&nbsp;<strong>enters</strong>&nbsp;from the right",
            "Everything in between stays the same"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "So instead of recalculating the whole sum, you just do&nbsp;<strong>one subtraction and one addition</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "<strong>Key insight:&nbsp;</strong>new_sum = old_sum − element_leaving + element_entering",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3-step-by-step-window-of-size-3",
      "title": "3. Step by Step: Window of Size 3",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Array:&nbsp;<code>[2, 5, 3, 8, 6, 1, 4]</code>&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; Window size k = 3",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 1:&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;compute the first window sum once:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785250878216-769805159.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": [],
          "content": null
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "window [0..2] → sum = 2+5+3 =<strong>10</strong>&nbsp;→&nbsp; max = 10",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 2:</strong>&nbsp;slide right: remove 2, add 8:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250879671-895033245.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250879671-895033245.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250879671-895033245.png",
          "alt": "Fixed window step 2, slide right"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "window [1..3] → sum = 10 − 2 + 8 =<strong>16</strong>&nbsp;→&nbsp; max = 16",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong></strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 3:</strong>&nbsp;slide right: remove 5, add 6:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785250881253-820200437.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": [],
          "content": null
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "window [2..4]Index&nbsp;<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">→ sum = 16 − 5 + 6 =</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">17</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;→&nbsp; max = 17</span>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong></strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 4:</strong>&nbsp;slide right: remove 3, add 1:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785250882763-385729472.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": [],
          "content": null
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "window [3..5]Index → sum = 17 − 3 + 1 =<strong>15</strong>&nbsp;→&nbsp; max = 17",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Step 5:</strong>&nbsp;slide right: remove 8, add 4:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785250884271-237333245.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": [],
          "content": null
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "window [4..6]Index → sum = 15 − 8 + 4 =<strong>11</strong>&nbsp;→&nbsp; max = 17 ✓",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Answer</b>:&nbsp;<strong>17</strong>&nbsp;(the window&nbsp;<code>[3, 8, 6]</code>). We never re-added the same elements twice.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3-the-template",
      "title": "3. The Template",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every fixed size sliding window problem follows the same 3-step pattern:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Build the first window:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">loop from index 0 to k−1 and compute the initial result</span><br>",
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Slide the window</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;loop from index k to n−1, add the incoming element and remove the outgoing element</span><br>",
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Track the answer</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;update your max/min/result after every slide</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>max sum of k consecutive elements</b>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint maxSumWindow(vector<int>& arr, int k) {\n    int n = arr.size();\n\n    // Step 1: build the first window\n    int window_sum = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        window_sum += arr[i];\n    }\n\n    int max_sum = window_sum;\n\n    // Step 2: slide the window\n    for (int i = k; i < n; i++) {\n        window_sum += arr[i];        // add incoming element\n        window_sum -= arr[i - k];    // remove outgoing element\n        max_sum = max(max_sum, window_sum); // track max\n    }\n\n    return max_sum;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    vector<int> arr = {2, 5, 3, 8, 6, 1, 4};\n    int k = 3;\n\n    cout << maxSumWindow(arr, k) << endl; // 17\n}\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Time complexity:&nbsp;<strong>O(n):&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;each element is added once and removed once.<br>Space complexity:&nbsp;<strong>O(1):</strong>&nbsp;no extra data structures needed.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4-fixed-window-identification-keywords",
      "title": "4. Fixed Window Identification Keywords",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "items": [],
          "url": "",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "{\"headers\":[\"Category\",\"Keywords / Phrases\"],\"rows\":[[\"Window Size Indicators\",\"size k, window of size k, length k, exactly k, fixed length k\"],[\"Subarray / Substring Indicators\",\"subarray of size k, substring of length k, substring of size k\"],[\"Consecutive Elements Indicators\",\"k consecutive elements, k contiguous elements, k continuous elements, k adjacent elements\"],[\"Window Processing Indicators\",\"every window, each window, for every window\"],[\"Subarray Processing Indicators\",\"for every subarray, for every substring\"],[\"Common Problem Statements\",\"maximum sum of k elements, minimum sum of k elements, average of k elements\"],[\"Window Query Problems\",\"maximum in every window, minimum in every window, first negative in every window\"],[\"Counting Problems\",\"count substrings of length k, count subarrays of size k\"]]}",
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "<p><strong>Quick rule:</strong></p><p>If the problem contains<strong>“k” + “consecutive / substring / subarray”</strong>, it usually indicates a<strong>Fixed Sliding Window</strong>problem.</p>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "Where You'll See This",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Maximum or minimum sum of k consecutive elements",
            "Average of every subarray of size k",
            "Maximum number of vowels in a substring of length k",
            "First negative number in every window of size k"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "<p></p><p><strong>Remember:&nbsp;</strong>Fixed size means k never changes. The window always contains exactly k elements it just moves.</p><p>If the window size can grow or shrink based on a condition, that's a&nbsp;<em>variable size&nbsp;</em>sliding window &nbsp;a different pattern.</p><p></p>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
